{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_001 asserts the §11.3 flags are a false positive by attributing them to 'inconsistent critic-version pinning' and an unreconciled version mismatch between frontier-claim-honest@v1 and the verdict-producing version in SRC_006. But SRC_001 lists zero commitments—no schema, no predicate, no program—so the claim is entirely unsubstantiated by machine-evaluable evidence. More critically, the very framing is self-defeating: if the harness pinned the wrong critic version, that is a harness-configuration defect, not a property of the artifact under audit. The target conflates an external evaluation-environment error with a substantive defense of its own content, offering no argument that the §11.3 flags are unwarranted on the merits of the audited material itself.","premise":"A defense against §11.3 adjudication-ritual flags must address whether the flags are substantively unwarranted for the artifact under audit, not merely assert that an unrelated version-pinning inconsistency elsewhere (SRC_006) caused a false positive.","target":"b0d1eb0b38c05de3357c8b31e50396557869948e9ce23f6245fb5c1fe1522188"}]}